==Trivia==
*It is unknown how all the [[Toons]] are capable of understanding Flutter despite the fact she never talks and only occasionally uses physical gestures (though in {{CI|Boxten|name=true}}'s case, his interaction with her either meant he can't understand what she's saying or her emotions are what was hard to understand about her). It is also unknown whether or not humans or non-Toon entities in general can understand her.
**Any dialogue she has that needs to be transcribed is always in the form of punctuation, like in a storyboard with her and {{CI|Dandy|name=true}}, in {{CI|Gigi|name=true}}'s lore tape, and in all of her dialogue, implying that Flutter cannot make ''any'' noise at all, other than from fluttering her wings.
***Flutter's dialogue has never once been translated into actual words and/or sentences for unknown reasons, and likely never will be.
*According to [[Dandy]]'s [[gossip]] about Flutter, she is able to sneeze despite her lack of a nose, further emphasizing the [[w:c:powerlisting:Cartoon Physics|cartoon logic]] all the [[Toons]] possess.
*Flutter's 3D model uses [[Dandy]]'s torso and legs, making her appear chubby. She has also frequently been drawn with a wider torso than most of the other female [[Toons]], which could imply this is her canon body shape.
*Flutter and her older brother {{CI|Flyte|name=true}} have numerous motifs and themes, whether similar or different, that establish their connection;
**Their names are ways of referring to a group of butterflies, and describing how they fly (a flutter and a flight).
**They have fur around their thoraxes, which is traditionally a trait moths have instead of butterflies.
**Their color palettes both involve the use of pink and turquoise.
**Their [[Twisted]] alternates never stop actively moving when roaming the map.
**Their body shapes and heights seem to add on to a duo trope where one member is short and plump, while the other is tall and lanky.
**Their Abilities involve spinning and boosting Movement Speed.
**Flutter is energetic and mostly peppy, while Flyte is more relaxed and laid-back.
*It's heavily implied Flutter can't use her wings as arms unlike Flyte, hence why she flies most of the time.
**A prominent example of evidence leading to this is that {{CI|Goob|name=true}} agrees to give hugs on her behalf because her wings are either too short, used too much for flying or cannot physically bend enough to wrap around anyone's bodies.
***Flutter also has a more rounded shape to her wings as opposed to Flyte's pointier, more avian wings. The pointed tips are likely better for articulation, possibly making it easier to grip onto things.
****In the [[poster]] art for the episode "Future and Past", Flutter can at least wave with her wings to greet others, as she does so to the viewer while up in a tree.
**As of the [[2026 Easter Event]], Flyte claims that he struggles to use his wings to hold a paintbrush (though likely only when it comes to painting small items, such as eggs), but he is talented at managing the (likely smaller) contents inside his {{TI|Scrapbook|name=true}}. He also claims that his wings are delicate when talking to {{CI|Yatta|name=true}}.
*Flutter is currently the only non-{{Type|Main}} [[Toon]] to need 100% [[Research]] on her {{CI|Twisted Flutter}}[[Twisted Flutter|Twisted counterpart]] to buy her.
*In her early concept art, Flutter used to have a {{wp|proboscis}}, a tongue-like organ that real butterflies use to suck nectar out of flowers. [[Twisted Flutter]]'s proboscis was turned into a snare trap in her concept art. As [[Twisted]] mechanics usually relate back to the original [[Toon]] in some way, this likely suggests that instead of constantly roaming the map at high speeds, Flutter's ability would've pulled Toons to her instead of lunging forward to fly faster, an ability that [[Goob]] has in the alpha release.
**Twisted Flutter hiding on a surface with her lower body being hidden is a trait {{CI|Twisted Squirm|name=true}} ended up receiving.
**[[Qwelver]] likely had no idea it's even called a proboscis when confirming Flutter does actually have a mouth after all, but even less likely meant she does truly have a legit mouth that cannot be seen on her design. Regardless of what was meant, Flutter has a mouth, one way or another.
*Flutter was almost [[scrapped]], but the staff liked her design so much that they brought her back, meaning she would have been the first Toon to be scrapped over how many staff members liked her.
*{{CI|Waxwell|name=true}} threatening to burn Flutter's wings likely marks the first depiction of what it looks like when she "screams". It is unknown whether she was furious or horrified at the time.
*Flutter and {{CI|Connie|name=true}} don't walk, but Flutter is the one who can walk if she wants<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/1251545388259741768/1342652352330600589</ref> as she has legs and Connie doesn't.
**Their respective siblings also have the ability to alternate between walking and flying (seen more prominently in their [[Twisted]] counterparts). [[Flyte]] in particular flaps his wings enough to not only form a tornado-like Gust of wind, but also propel himself off the ground for the duration of his wing movement. It is unknown if {{CI|Soulvester|name=true}} can fly even with his legwear and boots on, but as a {{CI|Twisted Soulvester}}[[Twisted Soulvester|Twisted]] he does due to not wearing them, exposing his ghostly tail in the process.
*Flutter and [[Gigi]] are close enough friends for the former to trust the latter to write in and hold onto her {{TI|Diary|name=true}} for her, but she disapproves of Gigi's thieving tendencies. Ironically, Flutter has never snitched or told on Gigi for it.
*Flutter was one of the few [[Toons]] who had their dialogue shown behind the scenes.
*One of her interactions with [[Connie]] reveals her favorite color is pink, but she gets upset when other people don't agree with her.
*Flutter and {{CI|Coal|name=true}} share the same [[Statistics]].
*Flutter is immune to the effects of the [[Ichor Leak]] [[Floor Event]] because she flies.
*Flutter is the cheapest {{Type|Rare}} [[Toon]] at 1300 [[Ichor]] solely when considering the currency; {{CI|Scraps|name=true}} is in second place at 1500.
*When Flutter got optimized in [[Changelog|v0.13.14]], she was given more mid-air animations, hovering higher off the ground and positioning one's username higher up than normal.
*Flutter and [[Flyte]] are the last semi-[[Event]] relative duo to receive a set of matching [[Skins]] in an Event Shop. In fact, they actually have two sets of matching [[Skins]] ({{Skin|Spring-Time}} and the Skins inspired by real-life moth species).
*Despite Flutter and {{CI|Shelly|name=true}} debuting in the same update, Shelly was designed after Flutter.<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/969934252844138499/1262809726681485413</ref>
*Flutter is the second non-[[Event Toon]] with a seasonal [[Gamepass]] [[Skin]], being part of the [[Spring-Time Cosmetic Pack]].
*Outside of gameplay, Flutter flaps her wings rapidly whenever feeling shock or other strong emotions. She does this to [[Gigi]] twice in the same lore tape focused on the latter (over Gigi's thievery tendencies and for taking a diary that wasn't hers, both implicitly). This is the first and currently only time Flutter's emotions can be understood via physical gestures and not just dialogue from others.
*There was a bug that affected her and the pet rocks where they would say [[Soulvester]]'s [[Ability]] dialogue while wearing his mask during the [[Haunted Gala]] [[Floor Event]]. While Pebble and Coal obviously can't talk at all due to being animal-coded, Flutter refuses to talk at all due to personal preference, so the bug was eventually fixed to prevent them from breaking character.

